# dotnet.config — repository-wide defaults for the `dotnet` CLI. INI format.
#
# The one setting here opts `dotnet test` into the native Microsoft.Testing.Platform
# (MTP) engine. xunit.v3 (Directory.Packages.props) is an MTP-native test framework:
# each test project builds as its own executable (`OutputType=Exe`) that speaks MTP's
# protocol directly. Starting with the .NET 10 SDK, `dotnet test` no longer bridges
# that to the legacy VSTest pipeline — it fails outright with "Testing with VSTest
# target is no longer supported by Microsoft.Testing.Platform on .NET 10 SDK and
# later", rather than silently doing the slow, wrong thing. This file is the
# documented opt-in to the replacement, applying to every `dotnet test` invocation
# under this directory: CI, the pre-commit hook, and a contributor's own machine
# alike, with nothing to remember per invocation.
#
# The corollary: `--logger "trx;LogFileName=x.trx"` (VSTest's logger syntax) is not
# something the native engine understands. Every CI workflow that wants a TRX file
# calls `--report-trx --report-trx-filename x.trx` instead, backed by the
# Microsoft.Testing.Extensions.TrxReport package both test projects reference.
# `--filter "FullyQualifiedName~X"` needs no change — xunit.v3's MTP filter
# implementation accepts the same expression syntax on purpose, for exactly this
# migration.

[dotnet.test.runner]
name = "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
